<http://data.silknow.org/object/25c05008-308a-33de-94d6-a686cd33b05d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Textile fragment of brocaded silk in coloured silks, France, 1730-1765"@en , "Textile fragment of brocaded silk. Off white silk with a floral pattern in coloured silks. There are sinuous green stems with seed pods and flowers, and a similar design in the ground of the silk is made by a self-coloured weft. The silk is made up from two fragments. Tabby with a slightly ribbed ground, owing to the flushing weft in every alternate shoot. The brocaded wefts are unbound."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c63c0c63-9fde-3f31-aace-cf1f821fdce2> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Textile fragment of brocaded silk in coloured silks, France, 1730-1765"@en , "Textile fragment of brocaded silk. Off white silk with a floral pattern in coloured silks. There are sinuous green stems with seed pods and flowers, and a similar design in the ground of the silk is made by a self-coloured weft. The silk is made up from two fragments. Tabby with a slightly ribbed ground, owing to the flushing weft in every alternate shoot. The brocaded wefts are unbound."@en ;
